# Shell scripts must reach the Linux box with LF endings.
#
# `scripts/deploy.sh` is executed by bash ON THE BOX. A CRLF checkout puts a
# stray \r at the end of every line and the deploy dies on the first one with an
# unreadable error. `backup-db.sh` and `restore-db.sh` run there too, through
# `npm run db:backup` / `npm run db:restore`.
#
# ── WHAT THIS DOES AND DOES NOT FIX (measured 2026-09-21) ───────────────────
# All three files are ALREADY stored LF-only in git — verified byte-wise, not by
# eye. This repo is developed on Windows with `core.autocrlf=true`, which
# normalises CRLF to LF on commit, so the blobs have always been clean.
#
# These rules make that guarantee EXPLICIT rather than a side effect of one
# machine's local config. `core.autocrlf` is per-clone and unset by default: a
# contributor without it commits whatever their editor produced, and for a file
# that only ever executes on a remote box, nothing local would catch it. That is
# the gap being closed here — not an existing breakage.
/scripts/deploy.sh     text eol=lf
/scripts/backup-db.sh  text eol=lf
/scripts/restore-db.sh text eol=lf
